    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nHi!\r\n\r\nFirts of all, I love what you're doing with mini.\r\n\r\nI'm just starting to convert my `nvim-treesitter-textobjects` config to use `mini.ai`.\r\n\r\nThe `custom_textobjects` work great, but I'm a bit stuck on implementing the `move` comands.\r\n\r\nSecifically, the ones below:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n      move = {\r\n        enable = false,\r\n        set_jumps = true, -- whether to set jumps in the jumplist\r\n        goto_next_start = { [\"]f\"] = \"@function.outer\", [\"]c\"] = \"@class.outer\" },\r\n        goto_next_end = { [\"]F\"] = \"@function.outer\", [\"]C\"] = \"@class.outer\" },\r\n        goto_previous_start = { [\"[f\"] = \"@function.outer\", [\"[c\"] = \"@class.outer\" },\r\n        goto_previous_end = { [\"[F\"] = \"@function.outer\", [\"[C\"] = \"@class.outer\" },\r\n      },\r\n```\r\n\r\n- `g[f` moves to the next function end, but how do I change it to go to the next function start instead?\r\n\r\nI'm probably missing something obvious here :)\r\n\r\n",
