            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks, Folke! That's a high praise coming from you :)\r\n\r\nTo be honest, moving cursor was mostly a tangential extra feature that required a relatively small addition to a codebase. So it is far from perfect and can't be a full replacement of 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects'.\r\n\r\nThe way default `g[`/`g]` work is essentially this: find corresponding whole `a` textobject using search direction from config and then move to its left/right edge. There is a slight difference when cursor is already on the edge of correct textobject: then it will find next one (with `count` bigger by one).\r\n\r\nSo `g[f` should find `af` textobject and move to its left edge. I am not sure why it is moving to function end instead. If it is indeed the case, I would be curious to see the config and text.",
